; pmwp.def - import declarations for the Workplace Shell parent classes
; that our sources and the sc-generated class-construction code reference:
;   wpobject.idl   dllname = "pmwp.dll";   (WPObject)
;   wpfsys.idl     dllname = "pmwp.dll";   (WPFileSystem)
;   wpdataf.idl    dllname = "pmwp.dll";   (WPDataFile)
;
; IMPORTANT: pmwp.dll exports nearly everything BY ORDINAL ONLY
; (unnamed entry slots - verified by dumping the system DLL).
; An import library built from NAME-based declarations links fine but
; FAILS AT LOAD TIME: the WPS silently refuses to load the DLL.
; The ordinals below come from Paul Ratcliffe's published "OS/2 PMWP.DLL
; Entry Points" table (home.clara.net/orac/os2/pmwp.htm), the same source
; proven correct by the AddrBook-Watcom port (its share.dll binds and
; runs against PMWP.14/15/23/26/27/32/315/323/326/327).
;
; Car's chain is WPObject <- WPFileSystem <- WPDataFile <- Car.  The
; generated construction code references the immediate parent's
; NewClass/ClassData symbols; grandparent entries are kept because the
; sc-generated parent-dispatch machinery may resolve through them, and
; an unused import costs nothing at load time (pmwp.dll is always
; resident inside the WPS anyway).
;
; Note the _wp*/_wpcls* methods need NO import entries at all: every
; method call goes through sc-generated dispatch macros reading the
; ClassData structures below, so only those structures and the NewClass
; factories are statically bound.
;
; Processed by IMPLIB into release\pmwp.lib (see Makefile.wat).  If
; wlink reports an unresolved symbol on a future build, look up its
; ordinal in Ratcliffe's table and add it here.

IMPORTS
   WPObjectClassData         = PMWP.23
   WPFileSystemClassData     = PMWP.11
   WPDataFileClassData       = PMWP.17
   M_WPObjectClassData       = PMWP.323
   M_WPFileSystemClassData   = PMWP.311
   M_WPDataFileClassData     = PMWP.317
   WPObjectNewClass          = PMWP.24
   WPFileSystemNewClass      = PMWP.12
   WPDataFileNewClass        = PMWP.18
   M_WPObjectNewClass        = PMWP.324
   M_WPFileSystemNewClass    = PMWP.312
   M_WPDataFileNewClass      = PMWP.318
